              "audioEnd": 139.262
            },
            {
              "text": "Children grew up listening to this tale, learning that being good always wins in the end.",
              "audioStart": 140.125,
              "audioEnd": 144.5
            },
            {
              "text": "They knew that truth and love would always guide their actions through every difficult day.",
              "audioStart": 145.363,
              "audioEnd": 149.363
            },
            {
              "text": "The country remained safe, and people lived in peace for generations.",
              "audioStart": 150.225,
              "audioEnd": 153.975
            },
            {
              "text": "The memory of the good son stayed in the hearts of all who heard the story.",
              "audioStart": 154.838,
              "audioEnd": 158.225
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Long ago, the king had ruled his land with care and wisdom.",
              "audioStart": 159.088,
              "audioEnd": 162.387
            },
            {
              "text": "He always made sure that his people had food and support.",
              "audioStart": 163.25,
              "audioEnd": 166.088
            },
            {
              "text": "When he grew old and weak, his heart filled with worry.",
              "audioStart": 166.95,
              "audioEnd": 169.762
            },
            {
              "text": "He knew that his kingdom needed a strong leader for the future.",
              "audioStart": 170.625,
              "audioEnd": 173.525
            },
            {
              "text": "His three sons were supposed to protect the country after he died.",
              "audioStart": 174.387,
              "audioEnd": 177.762
            },
            {
              "text": "However, the older two sons were unkind and full of pride.",
              "audioStart": 178.625,
              "audioEnd": 181.963
            },
            {
              "text": "They only cared about money and power for themselves.",
              "audioStart": 182.825,
              "audioEnd": 185.562
            },
            {
              "text": "The youngest son was different because he always showed kindness to everyone.",
              "audioStart": 186.425,
              "audioEnd": 190.075
            },
            {
              "text": "He helped people who were poor or sick.",
              "audioStart": 190.938,
              "audioEnd": 193.012
            },
            {
              "text": "When the wise man spoke about the water of life, the king listened closely.",
              "audioStart": 193.875,
              "audioEnd": 197.812
            },
            {
              "text": "He hoped that his sons would learn an important lesson during their travels.",
              "audioStart": 198.675,
              "audioEnd": 202.275
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "The journey was long and difficult for each brother.",
              "audioStart": 203.137,
              "audioEnd": 205.512
            },
            {
              "text": "Mountains stood tall against the sky, and roads were hard to follow.",
              "audioStart": 206.375,
              "audioEnd": 209.988
            },
            {
              "text": "The oldest brother rode fast because he wanted to find the water first.",
              "audioStart": 210.85,
              "audioEnd": 214.588
            },
            {
              "text": "He did not want to share the glory with anyone else.",
              "audioStart": 215.45,
              "audioEnd": 217.95
            },
            {
              "text": "When he met the small person on the mountain, he shouted at him.",
              "audioStart": 218.812,
              "audioEnd": 221.9
            },
            {
              "text": "The person became angry and used magic to trap him between the rocks.",
              "audioStart": 222.762,
              "audioEnd": 226.625
            },
            {
              "text": "The second brother made the exact same mistake.",
              "audioStart": 227.488,
              "audioEnd": 230.088
            },
            {
              "text": "He laughed at the little person and rode away quickly.",
              "audioStart": 230.95,
              "audioEnd": 233.637
            },
            {
              "text": "Soon, he was also trapped and unable to escape.",
              "audioStart": 234.5,
              "audioEnd": 237.412
            },
            {
              "text": "Both brothers learned that bad behavior leads to terrible problems.",
              "audioStart": 238.275,
              "audioEnd": 241.65
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Then the youngest son began his own trip.",
              "audioStart": 242.512,
              "audioEnd": 244.613
            },
            {
              "text": "Unlike his brothers, he stopped to talk to the small person.",
              "audioStart": 245.475,
              "audioEnd": 248.675
            },
            {
              "text": "He shared his bread and offered warm words of friendship.",
              "audioStart": 249.537,
              "audioEnd": 252.312
            },
            {
              "text": "The small person smiled and thanked the kind young man.",
              "audioStart": 253.175,
              "audioEnd": 255.887
            },
            {
              "text": "He told him where the castle was hidden in the dark forest.",
              "audioStart": 256.75,
              "audioEnd": 260.733
            },
            {
              "text": "The young man walked through the trees until he saw the ancient stone walls.",
              "audioStart": 261.595,
              "audioEnd": 265.257
            },
            {
              "text": "He used the stick and the bread pieces to open the heavy door.",
              "audioStart": 266.12,
              "audioEnd": 269.108
            },
            {
              "text": "Inside, the rooms were quiet and dark.",
              "audioStart": 269.97,
              "audioEnd": 272.27
            },
            {
              "text": "He found the water of life in a silver cup.",
              "audioStart": 273.132,
              "audioEnd": 275.37
            },
            {
              "text": "He filled his own bottle and started his journey back home.",
              "audioStart": 276.233,
              "audioEnd": 279.058
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "On his way out of the castle, he found his brothers stuck in the pass.",
              "audioStart": 279.92,
              "audioEnd": 283.582
            },
            {
              "text": "They looked tired and very sad.",
              "audioStart": 284.445,
              "audioEnd": 286.158
            },
            {
              "text": "The youngest brother did not leave them behind.",
              "audioStart": 287.02,
              "audioEnd": 289.345
            },
            {
              "text": "He used his own strength to help them get out of the rocks.",
              "audioStart": 290.207,
              "audioEnd": 292.97
            },
            {
              "text": "The older brothers felt ashamed of how they had treated him before.",
              "audioStart": 293.832,
              "audioEnd": 297.007
            },
            {
              "text": "They walked together as a family and talked about their mistakes.",
              "audioStart": 297.87,
              "audioEnd": 301.183
            },
            {
              "text": "When they finally reached home, the king was waiting for them.",
              "audioStart": 302.045,
              "audioEnd": 305.12
            },
            {
              "text": "He drank the water and stood up immediately.",
              "audioStart": 305.983,
              "audioEnd": 308.195
            },
            {
              "text": "Everyone in the country cheered and clapped for joy.",
              "audioStart": 309.058,
              "audioEnd": 311.558
            },
            {
              "text": "The king hugged his youngest son and thanked him for saving his life.",
              "audioStart": 312.42,
              "audioEnd": 315.882
            },
            {
              "text": "From that day on, the brothers lived together in peace and happiness.",
              "audioStart": 316.745,
              "audioEnd": 320.433
            }
          ]
        }
